Dear Hiring Team,

I am excited to apply for the *Software Engineer - Product* role at *Koah Labs*. I bring more than three years of experience taking end-to-end ownership of customer-facing systems, including a React and TypeScript workflow product used within a platform serving 10,000+ users. Koah's challenge - shaping core ad experiences that help publishers monetize and advertisers reach the right audience without compromising speed, UX, or privacy - is the kind of product and systems problem I want to own.

At Sperse, I shaped a React, TypeScript, and React Flow experience for creating, running, and managing agentic swarms, with Temporal providing durable execution and fast feedback loops. I also made critical technical decisions for a Python and FastAPI multi-agent CRM platform that routes requests across 40+ specialized agents with tenant-aware access control, communicating tradeoffs to technical and non-technical stakeholders. To make ambiguous workflows observable and reliable, I exposed 160+ validated backend actions through FastMCP, added Redis progress tracking, and used OpenTelemetry evaluations in CI/CD to test hypotheses about latency, accuracy, and safety before production releases. That combination of full-stack delivery, experimentation, and increasing autonomy directly matches Koah's need for engineers who can move across its core application and data systems while caring deeply about craft.

Earlier at Qualitest, I designed an end-to-end Java and Spring Boot storage service backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, with secure operations across AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage, and MinIO. I also optimized PostgreSQL data workflows and translated them into interactive React visualizations for business stakeholders, then improved error recovery for 100K+ weekly AWS Step Functions executions. These projects taught me to break down open-ended problems, validate decisions with performance evidence, and build reliable interfaces between product, data, and infrastructure - the same disciplines required to build AI-native advertising experiences at marketplace scale.

Koah's first-principles, positive-sum, and principled approach resonates with how I work: reason from evidence, communicate proactively, and make monetization improve the user experience rather than interrupt it. I would welcome the opportunity to bring that approach to Koah's high-trust team and help build the ad network for the next generation of AI-native products. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration; I look forward to connecting.

